senses.gloss:
विदः + .{@-दा@}
—1 Knowledge, learning.
—2 Understanding.

विदग्ध + .{@-ग्धः@}
—1 A wise or learned man, scholar; वृद्धा विदग्धाः प्रविशन्त्यत्र विप्राः Mb. 3. 133. 5.
—2 A libertine.

विदेह + .{@-हः@}
—1 The district Videha.
—2 N. of Janaka.

विद्रुत + .{@-तम्@}
—1 Flight.
—2 A particular manner of fighting.

विद्वेषणः + .{@-णम्@}
—1 Causing hatred or enmity; a kind of Tāntric rite.
—2 Enmity, hatred.
